FYDE: fix compiler warnings in upstream/downstream drivers

Silence several build warnings coming from the Raspberry Pi vendor
driver tree (not -Werror, but noisy and some indicate real latent bugs):

- dma/dw-axi-dmac: chan_flags_all was OR-accumulated without being
  initialized. Init to 0 (-Wuninitialized).
- media/rpi hevc_dec: hevc_d_device_run() could goto fail before src_req
  was assigned, then pass a garbage pointer to
  media_request_manual_complete(). Init src_req to NULL; the callee
  already WARN/returns on NULL (-Wsometimes-uninitialized).
- usb/dwc_common_port: the DWC_SPINLOCK_ALLOC() prototype was only
  declared in the non-CONFIG_DEBUG_SPINLOCK branch, so the definition
  had no visible prototype when spinlock debugging is on. Declare it
  unconditionally (-Wmissing-prototypes).
- pci/pcie-brcmstb: brcm_config_clkreq() does a read-modify-write of the
  HARD_DEBUG register but never read the current value first, leaving
  clkreq_cntl uninitialized and clobbering existing bits on write-back.
  Read the register first (-Wuninitialized).
- drm/vc4: vc4_async_setup_commit() is currently unreferenced; mark it
  __maybe_unused (-Wunused-function).

BUG=none
TEST=emerge-rpi5-openfyde sys-kernel/raspberry-kernel
